{
  "_readme": "Every shot of the pitch video. Times are in seconds. 'start' and 'end' are the planned times; when a shot has a 'cue', it instead starts the moment the narrator reaches those words (or the start of a line, written as @line_id), so the picture follows the voice. The first shot of each beat always starts on the beat. Beats are fixed at 0, 20, 40, 70, 100, 120. Edit cues, assets, labels and poses here; do not edit src/ unless asked for a design change. After editing run: npm run video:stills (inside tools/). Story shots: 'focus' is where the camera pushes toward, 'lights' are lamps that flicker and 'glow' is the phone, each as [x%, y%] of the picture; 'cover' lays a clean letter over a spot. Demo shots: 'rec' (a real recording in assets/recordings/) always wins; until it exists the real screenshot in 'screen' is shown, with a tap ring at each of 'taps' [x%, y%, seconds]. 'sfx' plays the app's own sounds: [file in assets/sfx/, seconds into the shot, volume 0 to 1].",
